       <item>
        <widget class="QLabel" name="cardReaderHelp">
         <property name="text"><string>The reader is read on this serial port (8 data bits, no parity, 1 stop bit). Put a card on it: its id shows on the Cards screen. The station's Arduino reader sends one line "CARD: &lt;id&gt;" for a card (9600 baud, ends with a line break): keep the text before the id as CARD: and lines of another kind are ignored. An original Arduino Uno shows up as /dev/ttyACM0, a clone with a CH340 chip as /dev/ttyUSB0.</string></property>
         <property name="wordWrap"><bool>true</bool></property>
